        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-a769ac8379f2d25c8c252a41",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Route of the Seven Lakes"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:25152ad0c634f823",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "bde7d9c6091e8d4c457fa639bf2cf61ab0118179200f22987c27836a5c042311",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-a769ac8379f2d25c8c252a41",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "The excursion takes about **8 hours**.\n\nThe Route of the Seven Lakes is one of the best-known drives in the Bariloche area. It covers about **300 km** and passes mountain peaks, beech forests, lagoons, waterfalls and blue lakes.\n\nAlong the way you'll pass Lago Escondido, the 'hidden lake'. Most of the route runs through Lanín and Nahuel Huapi national parks.\n\nThe scenery changes most visibly in autumn, when the beech forests turn red, orange and light brown."
    },
